+msgctxt "#33101"
+msgid "Copies what the diagnostics saved on this system (the folder hades-diag of its boot partition, every file of it through their filter already) to a USB drive that you choose, into its folder hades-diag, in a folder named after the date and time, and reads it back from the drive, file by file, before it says that it is there. Nothing on the drive is written over. It is for a system on a disk inside the PC, whose boot partition Windows does not show.[CR][CR]With nothing on the screen: in Windows, make a folder named hades-diag at the top of a USB drive, plug the drive in while this system is running, wait a minute and pull it out. The copy is in that folder."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33102"
+msgid "There are no diagnostics on this system to copy. They are saved while they are turned on: tick \"Save diagnostics there\" in the installer when you install or update, restart this system and wait five minutes."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33103"
+msgid "There is no USB drive to copy them to. Plug in one that Windows can read (FAT32, exFAT or NTFS), wait until this system shows it, and try again. A drive that is mounted read-only, or a disk inside the PC, is not offered."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33104"
+msgid "Copy the diagnostics to which drive?"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33105"
+msgid "%s free"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33106"
+msgid "Copying the diagnostics..."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33107"
+msgid "The diagnostics are on the drive, read back from it file by file, in the folder:"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33108"
+msgid "%s files. You can unplug the drive now. Look at them before you give them to anyone: no filter is perfect, and the README.txt in that folder says what each part is and what of it is personal."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33110"
+msgid "The diagnostics could not be copied."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33111"
+msgid "That drive cannot be used: it is no longer plugged in, or it is mounted read-only."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33112"
+msgid "There is not enough room on that drive."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33113"
+msgid "What was read back from the drive was not what had been written: the drive may be failing. Nothing was left on it: try another drive."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33114"
+msgid "The copy could not be written to that drive. Nothing was left on it."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33115"
+msgid "The diagnostics were busy writing for more than a minute, or another copy was being made. Try again."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33116"
+msgid "This system does not have enough free memory for the copy."
+msgstr ""
